0.02316758,-0.02671624,0.02611105,-0.05335441,-0.04505599,0.02121347,-0.09177318,0.04777498,0.01339495,-0.01095765,0.00884575,0.02999682,0.05704476,-0.03562276,0.0189219,0.00741451,-0.00309466,-0.02553209,0.1520184,0.04647118,0.01927447,0.06169411,-0.0301154,0.02980357,-0.00496022,0.02936052,-0.04049567,-0.00124996,0.06068262,-0.0382923,-0.02565329,-0.01504054,-0.04562489,0.05959382,0.06117331,0.03584316,0.03200454,0.03976223,-0.0184116,-0.02645202,0.10175477,-0.03596649,-0.04155868,-0.0802302,-0.04602271,0.0315993,-0.0219728,-0.00982602,-0.0171085,0.02987164,0.03732068,0.05055163,0.015787,-0.00571868,0.06665916,-0.05703144,0.03576096,0.00270879,-0.01424206,0.00293539,-0.0183662],"last_embed":{"tokens":472,"hash":"gsatme"}}},"last_read":{"hash":"gsatme","at":1785430518238},"class_name":"SmartSource","last_import":{"mtime":1785180470193,"size":21971,"at":1785430487811,"hash":"gsatme"},"blocks":{"#---frontmatter---":[1,10],"##No new hardware. No premium capacity. Just seven fixes any analyst can copy — and the one that alone cut the load time in half.":[11,32],"##No new hardware. No premium capacity. Just seven fixes any analyst can copy — and the one that alone cut the load time in half.#{1}":[13,32],"##First, Stop Guessing. Measure.":[33,54],"##First, Stop Guessing. Measure.#{1}":[35,44],"##First, Stop Guessing. Measure.#{2}":[45,45],"##First, Stop Guessing. Measure.#{3}":[46,46],"##First, Stop Guessing. Measure.#{4}":[47,48],"##First, Stop Guessing. Measure.#{5}":[49,54],"##Fix 1: The Data Model — Go Star Schema or Go Home":[55,72],"##Fix 1: The Data Model — Go Star Schema or Go Home#{1}":[57,72],"##Fix 2: Kill the Columns You’re Not Using":[73,84],"##Fix 2: Kill the Columns You’re Not Using#{1}":[75,84],"##Fix 3: Split DateTime, and Turn Off Auto Date/Time":[85,106],"##Fix 3: Split DateTime, and Turn Off Auto Date/Time#{1}":[87,106],"##Fix 4: Fix the Measures — Stop Making DAX Do the Model’s Job":[107,136],"##Fix 4: Fix the Measures — Stop Making DAX Do the Model’s Job#{1}":[109,136],"##Fix 5: Reduce What’s On the Canvas":[137,144],"##Fix 5: Reduce What’s On the Canvas#{1}":[139,144],"##Fix 6: Trim the Slicers and Interactions":[145,150],"##Fix 6: Trim the Slicers and Interactions#{1}":[147,150],"##Fix 7: If You’re on Fabric — Consider Direct Lake":[151,156],"##Fix 7: If You’re on Fabric — Consider Direct Lake#{1}":[153,156],"##What Didn’t Work (Because Something Never Does)":[157,166],"##What Didn’t Work (Because Something Never Does)#{1}":[159,166],"##The Results, By the Numbers":[167,179],"##The Results, By the Numbers#{1}":[169,170],"##The Results, By the Numbers#{2}":[171,171],"##The Results, By the Numbers#{3}":[172,172],"##The Results, By the Numbers#{4}":[173,173],"##The Results, By the Numbers#{5}":[174,174],"##The Results, By the Numbers#{6}":[175,175],"##The Results, By the Numbers#{7}":[176,179],"##Your Copy-Paste Checklist":[180,197],"##Your Copy-Paste Checklist#{1}":[182,187],"##Your Copy-Paste Checklist#{2}":[188,188],"##Your Copy-Paste Checklist#{3}":[189,189],"##Your Copy-Paste Checklist#{4}":[190,190],"##Your Copy-Paste Checklist#{5}":[191,191],"##Your Copy-Paste Checklist#{6}":[192,192],"##Your Copy-Paste Checklist#{7}":[193,193],"##Your Copy-Paste Checklist#{8}":[194,195],"##Your Copy-Paste Checklist#{9}":[196,197],"##The Bigger Picture":[198,209],"##The Bigger Picture#{1}":[200,209],"##FAQ":[210,225],"##FAQ#{1}":[212,225]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Sheth Priyanka","target":"Sheth Priyanka","line":5},{"title":"Split-screen Power BI performance cover: on the left a dark dashboard with a red stopwatch reading 14.0s and a spinning loading icon; on the right the same dashboard loading instantly with a green stopwatch reading 1.8s. Bold headline reads “14s to under 2s” with sub-stats: 7 fixes, 0 new hardware, 86% faster. The same report, the same data, the same laptop — before and after seven changes that live entirely inside the model and the DAX.","target":"https://miro.medium.com/v2/resize:fit:1400/format:webp/1*_JxOop8QHNB06UtNYu-DdA.png","line":13,"embedded":true},{"title":"Stylised Performance Analyzer panel showing a ranked list of visuals by duration. The top row, a matrix visual, is highlighted in red at 9,240 ms, broken into three coloured segments: DAX query 8,900 ms (large red), Visual display 210 ms (small amber), Other 130 ms (small grey). Below it, smaller bars for KPI cards and a line chart. A callout arrow points to the DAX query segment reading “This is where 90% of your time hides.”","target":"https://miro.medium.com/v2/resize:fit:1400/format:webp/1*Y8C4PagTNXbONWiljoowZw.png","line":39,"embedded":true},{"title":"Side-by-side data model comparison. Left, labelled “Before — flat table (slow)” in red: a single wide box listing 40+ mixed columns (SalesAmount, CustomerName, CustomerCity, ProductCategory, RegionName, Date, and more) with a red “12M rows x 42 cols” tag. Right, labelled “After — star schema (fast)” in green: a small central FactSales table with only keys and measures, connected by relationship lines to four compact dimension tables — DimCustomer, DimProduct, DimDate, DimRegion.","target":"https://miro.medium.com/v2/resize:fit:1400/format:webp/1*pyVMZ0JHcTUhNrdpugUFwA.png","line":63,"embedded":true},{"title":"VertiPaq column compression concept graphic on a dark background. Three vertical bars representing columns. Left bar labelled “Region (5 unique values)” is short and green, tagged “compresses great.” Middle bar “Order Date (365 values)” is medium and amber. Right bar “TransactionID (12M unique)” is very tall and red, tagged “compresses terribly — huge memory.” A caption strip reads: cardinality, not row count, drives model size.","target":"https://miro.medium.com/v2/resize:fit:1400/format:webp/1*-eHU_5Wz2f1e4xghvZW7cQ.png","line":77,"embedded":true},{"title":"separate post","target":"https://medium.com/towards-artificial-intelligence/i-tested-direct-lake-vs-import-vs-directquery-on-the-same-power-bi-dataset-one-silently-switched-b1f3104392f9","line":155},{"title":"Before-and-after horizontal bar chart on a dark background titled “Report load time.” Two bars: the top red bar labelled “Before” stretches to 14.0 seconds; the bottom green bar labelled “After” is a short stub at 1.8 seconds. A green badge on the right reads “86% faster.” Small footnote: same laptop, same data, no new hardware.","target":"https://miro.medium.com/v2/resize:fit:1400/format:webp/1*ecC7AoztBOdDYFqYNtiwWQ.png","line":176,"embedded":true},{"title":"Optimization checklist graphic styled as seven numbered cards on a dark background, each with a short label and an impact tag. 1 Measure with Performance Analyzer (find the real bottleneck). 2 Star schema, not flat tables (biggest win). 3 Remove unused + high-cardinality columns (~38% smaller). 4 Split DateTime and turn off Auto Date/Time. 5 Push heavy math upstream, keep DAX light. 6 Fewer visuals and slicers per page. 7 Consider Direct Lake on Fabric.","target":"https://miro.medium.com/v2/resize:fit:1400/format:webp/1*HJH0lrVN-YJjg_Qyjdg8vA.png","line":184,"embedded":true}],"metadata":{"title":"My Power BI Report Took 14 Seconds to Load. Here’s Everything I Did to Get It Under 2","source":"https://medium.com/towards-artificial-intelligence/my-power-bi-report-took-14-seconds-to-load-heres-everything-i-did-to-get-it-under-2-7ef5de8f5214","author":["[[Sheth Priyanka]]"],"published":"2026-07-24","created":"2026-07-27","description":"No new hardware. No premium capacity. Just seven fixes any analyst can copy — and the one that alone cut the load time in half.","Processed":"Unprocessed"},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[[93,105],[113,120],[126,129]],"key":"00.Inbox/My Power BI Report Took 14 Seconds to Load. Here’s Everything I Did to Get It Under 2.md"},
